      walkthrough = "Quest Started By: | Description:\n**Where:**\n- Chelsith Reborn [zone=914]\n**Who:**\n- Kilithyr [npc=43116]\nRating:\n0/0**_\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*_**\nInformation:\n**Level:** | 100\n**Maximum Level:** | 125\n**Monster Mission:** | No\n**Repeatable:** | Yes\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** | No\n**Quest Type:** | Task\n**Quest Goal:**\n- Advancement\n- Experience\n- Money\n**Quest Items:**\n- Bundle of Holy Symbols [item=110850]\n- Living Flame [item=110853]\n**Related Creatures:**\n- a calm matriarch [npc=43245]\n- a flame golem [npc=43199]\n- a new recruit [npc=43467]\n- a scheming noble [npc=43216]\n- a spiritspeaker [npc=43225]\n- a tranquil meditator [npc=43231]\n- a troubled seer [npc=43232]\n- a young shissar [npc=43240]\n- an adept metalworker [npc=43242]\n- an agitated matriarch [npc=43244]\n- an apprentice metalworker [npc=43248]\n- an escaped cultist [npc=43252]\n**Related Quests:**\n- Champions of the People [quest=6822]\n- Chelsith #1: Prove Your Worth, Slave [quest=6817]\n- Chelsith #2: How Puzzling All These Changes Are [quest=6818]\n- Chelsith #4: Ready The Killing Blow [quest=6820]\n- Unveiling the Mystery [quest=6821]\n**Era:** | !Rain of Fear\nRecommended:\n**Group Size:** | Solo\n**Min. # of Players:** | 1\n**Max. # of Players:** | 1\n**Appropriate Classes:**\n- All\n**Appropriate Races:**\n- All\nEntered: Wed Apr 17 16:58:30 2013\nModified: Wed Feb 28 02:53:00 2024 | | **Rain of Fear Information & Guides: An Overview \\| Group Progression & Task List \\| Raid Progression \\| Visible Armor**\n\n---\n\n_This is a solo task, the third task in a series of four. It begins with Kilithyr in the aqueduct area (findable with CTRL+F). He is at 1520, 50, 143._\n_To get to this area, you can jump down the well in the very far northeastern part of the zone or use one of the four portals scattered throughout the zone. For mapped locations, see the image on this NPC entry [npc=43146]._\n_Pre-Requisites:_\n\\- Level 85\n\\- Completion of \"Prove Your Worth, Slave\"\n\\- Completion of \"How Puzzling All These Changes Are\"\nYou say, 'Hail, Kilithyr'\nKilithyr says 'A fake city! Can you believe these dirty shissar have been holding us in a make-believe prison? The [scars] feel real enough.'\nYou say, 'What scars?'\nKilithyr says 'We've all bore our fair share of the bloody burden, and it's time we make the shissar bear theirs. If the people here are fake, we don't need to [hold back on our methods].'\nYou say, 'Hold back on our methods?'\nKilithyr says 'Think about it! If the shissar here [are not real people], then we should have no problem blowing them up with explosives.'\nYou say, 'They are not real people...'\nKilithyr says 'We don't actually know how many people are real here, but your tests in the residential area indicate that at least that section is fake. We'll focus [our efforts] on that part of town for now.'\nYou say, 'Our efforts?'\nKilithyr says 'We're going to raise hell and get the attention of whatever shissar is running this freak show. Get out there and make a scene, \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_.'\nYou have been assigned the task 'Hold Nothing Back'.\nThe news that the city you're trapped in is fake has convinced the slaves to no longer hold back in their attempts to break free. You've been tasked with causing as much mayhem to the populace as possible.\n\n---\n\n1\\. Collect cursed weapons from cultists 0/5 (Chelsith Reborn)\n_Task Window Says:_ Start by collecting weapons from the shissar, troll cultists, and a spiritspeaker hiding in the aqueduct. You can find them in the southern and eastern tunnels of the aqueduct.\n_Kill cultist mobs in the south and east tunnels of the aqueducts until you have five updates._\n\n---\n\n2\\. Kill metalworkers 0/5 (Chelsith Reborn)\n3\\. Place cursed weapons into equipment chests 0/5 (Chelsith Reborn)\n4\\. Collect hunks of living flame 0/8 (Chelsith Reborn)\n_Task Window Says:_ Head up to the surface and find the industrial area in the northwest part of the city. Kill the metalworkers building the shissar weapons and armor. Place the cursed weapons you stole into the equipment chests in the area, usually located near forges. And while you're there, collect hunks of living flame from the flame golems and flame arcanists working the forges.\n_Metalworkers are found in the industrial area ( map \\-\\- northwestern quarter of the zone, in and around the buildings)._\n_For the equipment updates, you just have to click on five of them. If you are part of a group getting these updates and all on the same step, they update automatically for everyone in your group. NOTE: When you do this, a non-aggro mob spawns and casts an AE knockback (this will break any invis buff)._\nYou slipped a cursed weapon into the equipment chest, where an unsuspecting Shissar is sure to grab it.\na new recruit punts you aside. 'Out of my way, ugly slave! I need to grab weapons before my patrol starts.'\na new recruit says 'What's happening? Ahhhhh!'\na new recruit crumples to the ground in sheer agony as the cursed weapons tear his flesh apart.\n_Flame golems and flame arcanists ( map) are found in the same area. This isn't an actual item; just a kill update. Upon the last one, you receive a \"Living Flame\"._\n\n---\n\n5\\. Collect holy relics from male shissar elders 0/8 (Chelsith Reborn)\n6\\. Kill shissar matriarchs 0/4 (Chelsith Reborn)\n7\\. Light shissar young on fire 0/12 (Chelsith Reborn)\n_Task Window Says:_ You must strike at the shissar in their homes if you really want to get Vyzh'dra's attention. Kill male shissar elders and rip the holy symbols off their clothes and jewelry. Kill shissar matriarches in their homes. Then use the living flame item you took from the industrial area to light the defenseless shissar young on fire. Don't let their cries dissuade you. Remember, everyone here is made from crystal, and not real.\n_Head to the residential area in the north-central part of the zone and kill any adult shissar in the area until you have eight updates (a scheming noble, a tranquil mediator and a troubled seer are some of the mobs that will update this step). Upon the last update, you receive \"Bundle of Holy Symbols\"._\n_Matriarches are found in the north-central part of the zone ( map)._\n_The young shissar (which are aggro-linked with their matriarch) are found in the same area. Use the \"Living Flame\" on the young shissar._\nThe living flame leaps from your fingertips and engulfs the shissar young in a ball of fire. The small shissar reverts to lifeless crystal and shatters under the heated pressure.\n\n---\n\n8\\. Throw the symbol package to cultists in the sewers 0/1 (Chelsith Reborn)\n_Task Window Says:_ Retreat back to the aqueducts and throw the shissar holy symbols you've found to a cultist or a necromancer in the south or eastern tunnels, by clicking the item in your inventory. With any luck, they'll use them to curse the shissar and demoralize them even further. Keep your distance though, the cultists are still dangerous.\n_With any shissar or troll cultist targeted (from a distance), right-click the Bundle of Holy Symbols._\nYou throw the bundle of shissar holy symbols to the cultist, who cackles wickedly.\nan escaped cultist says 'We'll curse a hundred shissar with these! But don't think this makes us friends, cretin.'\n\n---\n\n9\\. Speak to Kilithyr 0/1 (Chelsith Reborn)\n_Task Window Says:_ Find Kilithyr and report the results of your chaos quest to him.\nYou say, 'Hail, Kilithyr'\nKilithyr says 'If that doesn't get the attention of whoever's really in charge here, I don't know what will. Good work, \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_. And don't [feel bad].'\nYou say, 'Who says I feel bad?'\nKilithyr says 'In a normal city, these acts would be despicable. Here, we might as well be lighting bricks on fire. These crystal-beings don't have souls, no matter how real they look.'\nYou've sown chaos among the crystal-created populace of this Chelsith clone. You hope Kilithyr and Grulid know what they're talking about, because this is brutal violence.\n\n---\n\n_Rewards:_\nExperience (4 AAs + 2-3% regular exp at Level 100)\n300 platinum",
