      walkthrough = "Quest Started By: | Description:\n**Where:**\n- Chelsith Reborn [zone=914]\n**Who:**\n- Calvin Tresc [npc=43113]\nRating:\n0/0**_\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*_**\nInformation:\n**Level:** | 100\n**Maximum Level:** | 125\n**Monster Mission:** | No\n**Repeatable:** | Yes\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** | No\n**Quest Type:** | Task\n**Quest Goal:**\n- Advancement\n- Experience\n- Loot\n- Money\n**Time Limit:** | 06:00:00\n**Success Lockout Timer**: 06:00:00\n**Quest Items:**\n- Songspinner's Shoulderguard [item=111304]\n**Related Zones:**\n- Chelsith Reborn: Unveiling the Mystery [zone=916]\n**Related Creatures:**\n- Calvin Tresc [npc=43341]\n- Godslayer`s Illusory Reliquary [npc=43169]\n- Khozul, the Vanishing Serpent [npc=43375]\n- Portal Tender Kozath [npc=43343]\n- Portal Tender Srezek [npc=43345]\n- Portal Tender Vozesh [npc=43344]\n- Portal Tender Zureshek [npc=43342]\n- Szalvinzir, the Arena Champion [npc=43374]\n- Vhezush, the Stone Sentinel [npc=43376]\n- Vyzh`dra the Godslayer [npc=43384]\n- a battered toiler [npc=43352]\n- a broken slave [npc=43358]\n- a brutalizer [npc=43367]\n- a channeler [npc=43359]\n- a confused thrall [npc=43349]\n- a drunk toiler [npc=43369]\n- a flustered rebel [npc=43353]\n- a frozen fighter [npc=43361]\n- a livid torturer [npc=43366]\n- a mad captive [npc=43373]\n- a muddled laborer [npc=43350]\n- a muted miner [npc=43360]\n- a pained refugee [npc=43371]\n- a reanimator [npc=43357]\n- a resentful captive [npc=43368]\n- a revealed construct [npc=43355]\n- a scarred slaver [npc=43365]\n- a spireward [npc=43364]\n- a static servant [npc=43362]\n- a stoic refugee [npc=43363]\n- a sustainer [npc=43351]\n- a wounded servant [npc=43370]\n- an abused slave [npc=43372]\n- an enthralled rebel [npc=43356]\n- an unveiled apparition [npc=43354]\n**Related Quests:**\n- Champions of the People [quest=6822]\n- Chelsith #1: Prove Your Worth, Slave [quest=6817]\n- Chelsith #2: How Puzzling All These Changes Are [quest=6818]\n- Chelsith #3: Hold Nothing Back [quest=6819]\n- Chelsith #4: Ready The Killing Blow [quest=6820]\n- Raid Expedition: Champions of the People [quest=6839]\n- The Depths of Fear [quest=6924]\n**Era:** | !Rain of Fear\nRecommended:\n**Group Size:** | Group\n**Min. # of Players:** | 3\n**Max. # of Players:** | 6\n**Appropriate Classes:**\n- All\n**Appropriate Races:**\n- All\nEntered: Wed Apr 17 17:07:41 2013\nModified: Tue Dec 5 05:21:04 2023 | | **Rain of Fear Information & Guides: An Overview \\| Group Progression & Task List \\| Raid Progression \\| Visible Armor**\n\n---\n\n_This is a group mission that begins with Calvin Tresc in Chelsith Reborn (findable with CTRL+F). He is at the base of the giant tower (northwest side), at 1340, 885, 321 ( map)._\n_Pre-Requisites:_\n\\- Level 85\n\\- Completion of \"Prove Your Worth, Slave\"\n\\- Completion of \"How Puzzling All These Changes Are\"\n\\- Completion of \"Hold Nothing Back\"\n\\- Completion of \"Ready the Killing Blow\"\nYou say, 'Hail, Calvin Tresc'\nCalvin Tresc says 'Ah \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_, you've arrived, and not a moment too soon. Your name is on the forked tongue of every serpent in the city. Quite a grand place to be famous, or at least infamous, eh?' He surveys your expression and takes a more serious tone, 'Very well, I see you're as stoic as they say. The only way we're going to obtain victory here is to tear down the [veil] that blinds us from the truth.'\nYou say, 'What veil?'\nCalvin Tresc says 'As you've seen in your struggles here, the city is not what it seems. Manifestations of mad dreams take form and live among us. It is time we [reveal] the city for what it truly is: the machinations of a backstabbing beast.'\nYou say, 'Let's reveal it'\nCalvin Tresc says 'When you are [ready] I will open your eyes to the truth.'\nYou have been assigned the task 'Unveiling the Mystery'.\nAll of your heroic triumphs throughout the city have lead to this moment. Speak with Calvin Tresc and have him lead your charge into Vyzh`dra's seat of power.\n\n---\n\nSpeak with Calvin Tresc in the unveiled city 0/1 (Chelsith Reborn)\n_Speak with him and follow him._\nYou say, 'Hail, Calvin Tresc'\nCalvin Tresc says 'Look now at the unveiled city and see it for the sick stage that it is. The self titled 'Godslayer' is losing control of the strings he pulls to make these puppets dance. It is 'this' moment that we [strike] at the heart of his empire and free ourselves of this nightmare. Of course if this is all too much for you to handle you can [escape] reality and return to the charade.'\nYou say, 'Let's strike'\nCalvin Tresc says 'Vyzh`dra sits at the top of his [tower] waiting for our arrival. From what I can tell he's turned all of his attention to stopping our rebellion as he has forgone maintaining the charade of reality within the city. His puppets lie frozen and shattered in the streets. The only living creatures that seem to remain are his allies and ours.'\nYou say, 'What about his tower?'\nCalvin Tresc says 'The entrance to the top of his tower is guarded by four empowered servants. You will have to defeat them so that I can break the seal on the portal. The information I've gathered suggests that each guardian is shielded against both a school of magic and melee combat. Should one of them fall in battle the shielding is imparted on each of the other guardians. Your best bet is to kill them all concurrently. Give the word when you are [ready] to fight.'\nYou say, 'Ready!'\nCalvin Tresc charges as he shouts, 'Get rid of these guardians so that I may break the seal!'\n\n---\n\nStorm the Tower 0/1 (Chelsith Reborn)\n_When ready, just enter the tower._\nThe statuesque serpents spring to life and turn their attention toward you!\n\n---\n\nEliminate the Portal Guards 0/4 (Chelsith Reborn)\n_Task Window Says:_ Four loyal guardians are sustaining a shield around the portal to the top of Vyzh`dra's tower. Eliminate them. Beware that each portal guardian has a resistance against a school of magic and type of melee weapon. When a guardian dies, its immunities are shared among its remaining allies.\n_Each of the guards has a strength against a weapon type and spell type. When a guard is killed, they pass their strengths to the remaining guards:_\n\\- Portal Tender Kozath: slashing damage + disease/poison spells\n\\- Portal Tender Srezek: blunt damage + cold spells\n\\- Portal Tender Vozesh: piercing damage + fire spells\n\\- Portal Tender Zureshek: hand-to-hand damage + magic spells\n_The guards are permanently rooted and do not summon; however, if a guard is 10% health (or lower) than any other guard, they gain the ability to summon and begin casting a pull spell on their target._\n_As you kill them, you will see an emote:_\nAs the portal tender falls its strengths are shared with the remaining guardians.\n_Upon the death of the last Portal Tender, you see:_\nCalvin Tresc shouts excitedly, 'Yes, that's it! Your sick game is over 'Godslayer'!' He looks over and beckons you toward the portal, 'Speak to me when you are ready and we shall confront the snake directly.'\n\n---\n\nSpeak with Calvin Tresc again 0/1 (Chelsith Reborn)\nYou say, 'Hail, Calvin Tresc'\nCalvin Tresc steps into the portal with a smug look on his face.\nCalvin Tresc turns back, a look of dire concern on his face, 'Impossible, the tower portal is inactive! That must mean...' His words trail off as his voice is but a whisper to the bellow that interrupts him.\nThe serpentine voice of the dominion's master hisses loudly throughout every corner of the city, 'Do you really expect to essscape this place, Tresc?'\nCalvin Tresc shouts, 'Go now and gather our allies together! No doubt the Godslayer's minions have set out to squash the rebellion.'\n\n---\n\nGather allies out where the World Ends 0/3 (Chelsith Reborn)\n_Task Window Says:_ Reconvene with Belissa the Barker to the north out where the world ends. The shissar have moved to suppress any resistance members in that area.\nYou say, 'Hail, Belissa the Barker'\nBelissa the Barker says 'Just in time savior! These conjurors have been sent by Vyzh`dra to squash our little going away party. If you would be so kind as to kill them and their little crystal projections off I'm sure we'll all be one step closer to getting what we want.'\n_In the very far northern part of the zone are three groups of slaves. Kill all the KOS NPCs around them. Note that the shissar sustainers summon time-based adds (two at a time), so you will want to focus on killing them first. You'll see this emote as they summon adds:_\nThe shissar sustainer raises its arms into the air and conjures two more allies to aid in the fight!\n_Upon the death of the last mob:_\nBelissa the Barker calls out to you gratefully, 'That's the last of 'em. I'll wait for you at the center square.'\nBelissa the Barker roars at the remaining resistance members, 'Pack it up you lazy lot and get to the center. We've got a war to win!'\n\n---\n\nGather allies from the Aqueducts 0/6 (Chelsith Reborn)\n_Task Window Says:_ Find Kilithyr in the aqueducts below the city and rescue any remaining resistance members that may still be alive.\nYou say, 'Hail, Kilithyr'\nKilithyr says 'You're just in time, savior. A gang of Vyzh`dra's brutes have started exterminating the survivors here. Flush them out so the resistance can put an end to this nightmare. Go now, quickly!'\n_In the aqueducts, do the same thing for the six groups of slaves there. To get to the aqueducts, you can jump down the well in the far northeastern part of the zone (note that the well area is full of mobs, so you will probably get this task step update last)._\n_Mobs in the aqueducts tend to hit for a max ~17,500. Upon the death of the last mob:_\nKilithyr calls out to you, 'That's the last of the brutes down here. I pray that the gods look favorably upon you as you enter the tower.' His voice grows quieter, '...I have a bad feeling about this.'\n\n---\n\nGather allies from the Pit 0/4 (Chelsith Reborn)\n_Task Window Says:_ Meet up with Grulid near the great spires in the northeast. Several shissar reanimators are using the spires to amplify Vyzh`dra's powers over the city.\nYou say, 'Hail, Grulid'\nGrulid speaks in a whisper, 'Good, you've arrived. These necrotic enchanters have trapped my battalion in some sort of stasis using the power of these pillars. I believe slaying them will lift the veil on the monuments and free our allies from their grasp.'\n_Around the well in the far northeastern part of the zone are four groups of Shissar. Note that these appear to be aggro-linked in groups of three. Kill all of them to free the slaves in this area._\n_As you kill mobs, you'll see emotes:_\nThe western spire shakes violently and breaks into pieces, revealing its true nature.\nThe great crystal shatters into pieces, weakening Vyzh`dra's illusion.\nThe southern spire shakes violently and breaks into pieces, revealing its true nature.\nThe mighty shard loses its power and falls to the ground, lifeless.\nThe eastern spire trembles and cracks slightly.\nThe eastern spire shakes violently and breaks into pieces, revealing its true nature.\nThe giant crystal explodes in a shower of deadly pieces.\nThe northern spire trembles and cracks slightly.\nThe northern spire shakes violently and breaks into pieces, revealing its true nature.\nThe enormous shard fractures into tiny pieces, loosening the shissar's hold on your allies.\nAs the final crystal spire shatters into pieces the frozen resistance members regain control of their bodies.\nGrulid joyfully exclaims, 'I knew from the day we first met that you would be our savior. I shall rally these troops in the center of town and await your arrival there!'\n\n---\n\nMeet your allies at the center of the city 0/1 (Chelsith Reborn)\n_This updates in the city center (north of the arena, where the giant statue is)._\nVyzh`dra's voice fills every corner of the city, 'How is it you expect to defeat me in my own domain!? Does your power blind you from even the sssimplest truths in front of your eyes?'\nVyzh`dra continues, 'Look around you. You would lay down your lives for these soulless vessels? There is no victory for you here.'\nThe fear tainted sky parts, revealing Norrath in the distance.\nVyzh`dra speaks, 'A final obstacle for you to overcome if you truly wish to join me in my tower.' Your attention shifts toward the stone statue in the center of the pool.\n\n---\n\nDefeat Vhezush, the Stone Sentinel 0/1 (Chelsith Reborn)\n_Task Window Says:_ Vyzh`dra's power over the city has not yet been severed. He has animated the statue in the center of town to protect the portal to his seat of power. Destroy the final portal guardian!\n_Note that Vhezush gains strength as he lowers in health:_\nThe stone sentinel crumbles, becoming more susceptible to damage but more dangerous in combat.\n_At its worst (under 10% health), it hits for a max ~30,000 (possibly even higher). Kill it to update this step:_\nVhezush, the Stone Sentinel has been slain by \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_!\nThe ground shakes as the stone sentinel falls dead. A portal has opened at the base of its pedestal.\nVyzh`dra's speaks slowly, you are unsure if he is furious or simply toying with you, 'Clearly I should have known I was not safe even in my own domain from such mighty conquerors. Please, join me at the top of my tower and I shall lay down my arms and shower you in the treasure you so clearly deserve.'\n\n---\n\nStep through the newly opened portal 0/1 (Chelsith Reborn)\n_Task Window Says:_ With the stone sentinel defeated, the portal to Vyzh`dra's seat of power is open. Step through the portal north of the statue's pedestal.\n_NOTE: Once the portal is activated, your group is ported into the tower. Once in the tower, you will not be able to return, so if you're going to engage either of the two optional nameds in the zone, don't port in yet._\n_Enter the portal to Vyzh`dra's tower._\nA flash of light blinds you as \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_ activates the tower portal. You open your eyes to see the dominion's master standing over you.\nVyzh`dra looks down at your party with aloof contempt. He speaks with a mocking tone, 'Thisss is the army you've gathered to dethrone me?'\nGrulid grips his weapon tightly as he glares at the empowered shissar.\n\n---\n\nConfront Vyzh`dra at the top of his tower 0/1 (Chelsith Reborn)\nVyzh`dra the Godslayer grips his blade tightly and swings it high over your head. You are confused by Vyzh`dra's hysterical laughter until you look around the room. A quick survey reveals that most of your party is either dead or lumps of lifeless crystal!\nVyzh`dra the Godslayer shouts 'As I said, there is no victory for you here. You fight for soulless projections of my imagination. Even when you hurt me most, you did it for me. There is no hope for you. No reward, no fanfare, no accolades to be won or noble creatures to save. You have willingly marched into the depths of misery and death to share in just a fraction of my personal torment. How does it feel to have those you care for, those you fought so hard to defend, suddenly fall dead with barely a whimper? It hurt me a hundred times more.'\nVyzh`dra the Godslayer looks you over carefully, 'You have changed greatly since our first meeting. Then again, so have I. That brittle broken body you put to rest time and time again is a distant memory of my power now. I bet you don't even know how I came to be the subject of your torture.'\nVyzh`dra the Godslayer continues, 'I aimed to usurp that false emperor, but was stopped by turncoats and backstabbers who had lost sight of our peoples' purpose. Those miserable snakes sit in solitude waiting for your kind to march in and pillage all they own. Not I, though. I am above such complacency. Look around you and see the fruits of my labor. Ssraeshza thought binding my body to the depths of the temple so that it could be slain by your kind time and time again was a fitting punishment. Yet now, now that my soul has escaped and claimed the power of that bastard that drove us from Norrath, I am stronger than he could ever dream to be!'\nThe portal in the center of the room begins radiating with power. Vyzh`dra has allowed you to exit.\nVyzh`dra the Godslayer looks to the fear shard suspended at the center of the temple, 'So cliche, to expound at length before doing away with you.' He pauses then smiles, 'Let us play a more fitting game. I shall let you live, to fester in your revelations, and I shall wait at the coliseum. When you are ready to end your lives, speak with Kilithyr. I will allow him to wake from this dream, conscious of the truth. But I'll send the rest of this lot back to their supposed lives with no memory of what happened here. Just so I can watch the baffled look on their faces when you try to explain all of this to them...'\nWith that, the mighty serpent vanishes and a chest of treasures is revealed as a mocking reward.\n\n---\n\nClaim your treasure 0/1 (Chelsith Reborn)\n_Task Window Says:_ Claim the treasures that Vyzh`dra has left for you.\nAll of your endeavors to rescue the people of this city have proved to be a sick joke. Vyzh`dra has allowed you to live and return to the oblivious population of his illusionary city. He departed offering you a final challenge, seek Kilithyr if you wish to do battle with the Godslayer in his arena.\n\n---\n\n**Optional Encounters**\n(Optional) Defeat Szalvinzir, the Arena Champion 0/1 (Chelsith Reborn)\n_Task Window Says:_ One of Vyzh`dra's champions awaits anyone who would challenge him in the great coliseum.\n_This is an optional fight in the arena. Killing it will gain you an extra item in the reward chest. The fight occurs in five phases:_\nPhase 1: Szalvinzir, the Arena Champion (Lvl: 100)\nPhase 2: Szalvinzir the Great (Lvl: 101)\nPhase 3: Szalvinzir the Mighty (Lvl: 102)\nPhase 4: Szalvinzir the Revealed (Lvl: 103)\nPhase 5: Stone Memory of Szalvinzir (Lvl: 104)\n**Details:**\nPhase 1: Throughout the fight, spawns a large number of \"a hissing serpent\" (Lvl: 75) which are very weak with low HP. If you burn him down before any serpents spawn, you will get the I Love Snakes achievement.\nPhase 2: Throughout the fight, spawns \"a bladestorm\" (Lvl: 98) one at a time. We ended up with 5 or 6. They hit for up to 8000.\nPhase 3: Occasionally Szalvinzir will lock HP and a trap will spawn. Drag Szalvinzir over the trap to resume killing.\nPhase 4: Crystal form. Nothing special.\nPhase 5: During the fight, spawns \"a shissarian nightmare\" (Lvl: 98) one at a time. 4 total. They hit for up to 10000.\nThe event can be reset by moving outside the arena.\n(Optional) Defeat Khozul, the Vanishing Serpent 0/1 (Chelsith Reborn)\n_Task Window Says:_ An ancient spy of Vyzh`dra is one of his last living allies. You will find him on the southwestern shore of the beach, contemplating his return to Luclin.\n_This is an optional fight in the beach area - far southwestern part of the zone. Killing it will gain you an extra item in the reward chest._\n_Khozul AE rampages and flurries, and casts \"Assassin's Repulse\" (random single target):_\nAssassin's Repulse: Single Target, Unresistable (0)\n1: Stun (2.40 sec/999)\n2: Decrease Hitpoints by 57693\n_At 80%, 60%, 35%, 25%, 15%, and 5%, he turns invisible (he keeps attacking) and buffs himself with two 2-tick buffs:_\nKhozul steps into the shadows and surrounds himself with a reflective aura.\nShadowy Reflection: Self 0', Unresistable (0)\n1: Increase Chance to Reflect Spell by 100%\n2: Increase Absorb Magic Damage by 100000000\nShadowy Spikes: Self 0', Unresistable (0)\n1: Mitigate Melee Damage by 100%, 100000000 total\n11: Increase Damage Shield by 10000\n_Turn off attacks and wait for him to return to Shissar form before resuming._\n\n---\n\n_Rewards:_\nExperience (3 AAs + regular experience)\n225 platinum\n_Possible Chest Loot (1 item + 1-3 items per task):_\nChain Wrapped Gorget\nCloak of the Battlefield\nFine Linen Facewrap\nIron Chain Earring\nLimestone Oddity\nMask of the Slain\nMirage Loop\nResonant Cord\nSilk Shissar Drape\nSlave's Final Companion\nSongspinner's Shoulderguards\nThrumming Violet Shard\nVeil of Sacrifice\nVisor of Triumph\nLesser Dreadmote\nMedian Dreadmote\nGreater Dreadmote\nGlowing Dreadmote\nThis also drops a \"Strange Black Rock\" - used in the **Depths of Fear** [quest=6924] class-specific weapon achievement.\n- Chain Wrapped Gorget [item=111146]\n- Cloak of the Battlefield [item=111246]\n- Fine Linen Facewrap [item=111145]\n- Glowing Dreadmote [item=106497]\n- Greater Dreadmote [item=106464]\n- Iron Chain Earring [item=111185]\n- Limestone Oddity [item=111203]\n- Mask of the Slain [item=111186]\n- Median Dreadmote [item=106509]\n- Mirage Loop [item=111229]\n- Resonant Cord [item=110964]\n- Silk Shissar Drape [item=111147]\n- Slave's Final Companion [item=111204]\n- Strange Black Rock [item=56895]\n- Thrumming Violet Shard [item=110851]\n- Veil of Sacrifice [item=111183]\n- Visor of Triumph [item=111228]",
